@* One "Add" button had to become a question, because the page holds two things
   you can add and they are a level apart: a PROCESS is a card in the flow strip,
   a STEP is a row inside the one you are reading.

   Two full-width choices rather than a menu. MudMenu has swallowed clicks in
   this codebase before - a button nested in its activator stops working - and
   this is the kind of thing that must not silently fail. *@

<MudDialog>
    <TitleContent>
        <div class="app-addchooser__title">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Size="Size.Small" />
            <span>What would you like to add?</span>
        </div>
    </TitleContent>

    <DialogContent>
        <div class="app-addchooser">

            <button type="button"
                    class="app-addchooser__choice"
                    @onclick="@(() => Choose(AddChoice.Step))">
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.FormatListNumbered"
                         Class="app-addchooser__icon" />
                <span class="app-addchooser__name">A step</span>
                <span class="app-addchooser__what">
                    Another row inside <strong>@ProcessName</strong> - a thing somebody
                    does, with the people responsible and a screenshot.
                </span>
            </button>

            <button type="button"
                    class="app-addchooser__choice"
                    @onclick="@(() => Choose(AddChoice.Process))">
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.AccountTree"
                         Class="app-addchooser__icon" />
                <span class="app-addchooser__name">A process</span>
                <span class="app-addchooser__what">
                    A new card in <strong>@FolderName</strong>, with its own steps
                    underneath it.
                </span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </DialogContent>

    <DialogActions>
        <MudButton OnClick="Cancel">Cancel</MudButton>
    </DialogActions>
</MudDialog>
